  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative led by Marcus Cole, launching in Q3 2023 with a kickoff on July 15th. The project aims to enhance security and accessibility using AI. Key milestones include an initial findings report in August highlighting a potential 20% efficiency increase, a team expansion adding members in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, and machine learning, and the completion of the design phase leading into development under lead developer Omar Jensen. The team is also gathering AI-driven data visualization ideas, celebrating the completion of the testing phase in October, and seeking stakeholder feedback on the prototype by November. Additionally, a $15,000 budget has been approved for specialized training."
